.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-onboardings - Onboarding requests: list, invite, correct, resend, cancel (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin onboardings [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the onboarding requests: the invites an operator sent and the sign-ups merchants
made themselves, each with its state, how its last email went, and its clashes with
accounts or with other requests (conflicts).

.PP
Open and expired requests are listed by default: the ones still waiting for something.
--status completed shows the history; a completed request's id is its account's id.

.PP
A request becomes an account only when the merchant claims it, by signing with the
wallet it names, from the link in the email. The link is never shown here.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for onboardings

.PP
\fB--origin\fP=""
	Only requests from this entrance: operator (an invite) or signup (self-service)

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--send-failed\fP=""
	Only requests whose last email failed ('true') or did not ('false')

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by created_at, expires_at, last_sent_at, name or email (prefix - for descending; default: newest first)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	State(s), comma-separated or repeated: open, expired, completed (default: open,expired)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin onboardings
  rail0 admin onboardings --send-failed true        # whose email did not go out
  rail0 admin onboardings --status completed --origin signup --pretty
  rail0 admin onboardings invite --name "Acme Store" --email ops@acme.example --address 0x2D2B…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-onboardings-cancel(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-onboardings-correct(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-onboardings-invite(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-onboardings-resend(1)\fP
